<title>UK: Concentric shares jump after CEO news.</title>
<headline>Concentric shares jump after CEO news.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Concentric Plc jumped on Wednesday after the UK machinery equipment manufacturer announced the appointment of John Towers as new chief executive from October 1.</p>
<p>The former chief executive of the Rover Group, Towers replaces Robert Bruce who remains with the group as a director of Concentric Overseas Ltd.</p>
<p>Towers resigned from Rover in April.</p>
<p>By mid-morning, the shares were 29p higher at 198-1/2p, a rise of 17 percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
